Composer

Composer is a dependency manager for PHP applications. This powerful tool makes working with code easier.
For example, Composer can be used to install an HTTP client package, which will simplify interaction with our API.
Here is an example of connecting the Composer autoloader in a recipe:
PHP
<?php

require_once '/path/to/autoload.php';
Next, Composer will help you load the classes needed in your scripts.

HTTP client

symfony/http-client component is a low-level HTTP client that provides utilities to consume APIs.
Here's how we use this client in our recipes:
PHP
<?php

require_once '/path/to/autoload.php';

// Just instantiate a known client (thanks to Composer autoloading)
// by static factory method, with required options
$client = \Symfony\Component\HttpClient\HttpClient::create([
    'base_uri' => 'api.systeme.io/api/',
    'headers' => [
        'X-API-Key' => 'your_secret_api_key',
        'Content-Type' => 'application/json',
    ]
]);

...

require_once '/path/to/autoload.php';

const API_KEY = 'your_secret_api_key';

$client = \Symfony\Component\HttpClient\HttpClient::create([
    'base_uri' => 'api.systeme.io/api/', // Base API URI
    'headers' => [
        'X-API-Key' => API_KEY, // Your API key
        'Content-Type' => 'application/json', // Default content type
    ]
]);

$contactCreatedResponse = $client->request('POST', 'contacts', [
    'body' => json_encode([
        'email' => ' [example@email.com](mailto:example@email.com) ',
        'locale' => 'en',
        'fields' => [
            [
                'slug' => 'country',
                'value' => 'FR',
            ],
            [
                'slug' => 'phone_number',
                'value' => '123456',
            ],
        ],
    ]),
]);
